+| 22 | `crates/anvilml-hardware/tests/mock_tests.rs` buildable without `mock-hardware` | (pre-existing since the test file's own authoring; not traced to a single task) | The file unconditionally imports `anvilml_hardware::mock::MockDetector` at module scope, but `mod mock` is itself `#[cfg(feature = "mock-hardware")]`-gated in `lib.rs`. Unlike its sibling `detect_tests.rs` (same crate), which mixes always-on tests with individually `#[cfg(feature = "mock-hardware")]`-gated functions and has no unconditional import of the gated module, `mock_tests.rs` is 100% mock-only content with no such guard anywhere. CI never caught this because every documented CI/local workflow passes `--features mock-hardware` explicitly (`ANVILML_DESIGN.md §18.3`, `ENVIRONMENT.md §2`); a plain `cargo test --workspace` with no feature flags — a reasonable thing for a developer to run — fails with `E0432: unresolved import`. | Manual retrofit patch (not a numbered task) — added a `[[test]]` target for `mock_tests` in `anvilml-hardware/Cargo.toml` with `required-features = ["mock-hardware"]`, so Cargo skips building this specific test binary when the feature is off instead of erroring; other auto-discovered test targets in the crate are unaffected |
 
 All nineteen are closed in the current task graph and source tree as of this document's generation. Items 1–10 are retrofit tasks in Phase 900 (completed phases P1/P3/P6 cannot be edited directly per project convention — fixes for defects in completed phases always land in P900). Items 11–15 are in-phase corrections to Phase 8, Phase 18, and Phase 17 respectively, since none of those phases had executed yet when found — the fix lands in the phase that owns the gap rather than in a retrofit. Items 16–19 are direct source-code retrofit patches to completed code (`P8-E3` for 16-18, `P7-B2` for 19), applied outside the numbered task sequence (the same category as commit `0fdf3e9`) rather than as new tasks. Item 19 is the sole exception to the "documentation-vs-implementation correction, no design decision to make" characterization of 16-18 — it required a genuine synchronization redesign (the `watch`-channel signal), not just writing the code a comment already promised; it is included here rather than deferred to a dedicated Phase-7 task because `P8-E6`'s upcoming respawn loop depends on multi-generation crash simulation that would otherwise inherit this exact deadlock risk on day one.

